@attribute [Route(GuestSignInRegistration.VerifyPath)]
@using NFHotel.Web.Security
@inherits NFHotel.Web.Common.CancellableComponentBase

@inject BookingVerifyViewModel ViewModel
@inject NavigationManager Navigation

@*
    The page of the link in the mail of a booking request (MIL-088, ADR-0052 decision 3). The link is
    /booking/verify#<token>: the token stands after the #, which a browser never sends, so no access log holds it.

    A static server-rendered page with one form and one button, with no @@rendermode, like the sign-in: only the answer
    to a request can set the guest cookie. Opening the link changes nothing: the page renders the form and calls no one,
    so a mail scanner that opens the link books nothing. The script of the page, a file of the site's own because the
    Content Security Policy refuses inline code (MIL-033), copies the token from the address into the hidden field, takes
    it out of the address bar, enables the button and disables it once it is pressed. Only the button sends the token: a
    POST with the token and the antiforgery token in its body, which the web application passes to the API in the body
    (ASVS 3.5.3 and 14.2.1). Without script the field stays empty, the button stays disabled, and the page says why.

    The answers of the page carry Referrer-Policy: no-referrer and Cache-Control: no-store (VerifyPageHeaders). A press
    that books the room signs the guest in as the sign-in does and sends the browser to the guest's own booking, which
    shows the receipt with the reference; a reload there shows it again and does not press the button again.

    PublicLayout is the default layout (Routes.razor), so there is no @@layout line.
*@

<PageTitle>Book your room — NFHotel</PageTitle>

<div class="pub-section">
    <div class="pub-wrap">
        <div class="pub-booking stack-lg">
            <PageHeader Title="Book your room"
                        Subtitle="Press the button to book the room you asked for." />

            <ErrorAlert Errors="ViewModel.Errors" />

            @if (ViewModel.HasFailed)
            {
                <p>
                    <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/book">Go to the booking page</a>
                </p>
                <p class="muted">
                    Already booked? <a href="@GuestSignInRegistration.SignInPath">Find your booking</a> with the booking
                    reference from our email and the email you booked with.
                </p>
            }
            else
            {
                <form method="post" @formname="@FormName" @onsubmit="VerifyAsync" id="booking-verify-form" class="card card-pad stack">
                    <AntiforgeryToken />
                    <input type="hidden" id="booking-verify-token" name="@TokenField" />

                    <p>
                        Your room is booked when you press the button, not before. The link in the email works once.
                    </p>

                    <noscript>
                        <div class="alert alert-error">
                            <p>
                                This page needs JavaScript to book your room. Turn JavaScript on, then open the link in the
                                email again.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </noscript>

                    @* Shown by the script when the address has no token. The class sets no display, so hidden holds. *@
                    <div id="booking-verify-missing" class="alert alert-error" role="alert" hidden>
                        <p>
                            This address has no link to book with. Open the link in the email again, or ask for the
                            booking again on the <a href="/book">booking page</a>.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="row">
                        <button type="submit" id="booking-verify-button" class="btn btn-primary" disabled>Book the room</button>
                    </div>
                </form>
            }
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<script src="@Assets["js/booking-verify.js"]"></script>
